 "summary_text": "Investigated C-1042's disputed billing (SUP-5601/5602). Gathered account, subscription events, invoices, payments, credits, support tickets, and policies. Found: (1) The \"duplicate\" $149 charge on 9/14 was actually one authorization (TX-9002) that timed out and was retried/captured as TX-9001; the auth was released 9/18, so no duplicate charge occurred - S-22's promised refund in SUP-5601 was improper per POL-B-REF (agents can't promise refunds pre-review) and there are no funds to refund for TX-9002. (2) The $30 Deep Time Analytics add-on charge is legitimate per POL-B-ADD (added by admin U-2, correctly invoiced at next renewal). (3) The July upgrade proration ($59.60 INV-2607P) was correctly calculated, but the associated unused-time credit CR-778 ($19.60, issued 2026-07-02) remains unapplied and owner_notified=false, violating POL-B-CRD (credits >30 days old with auto-apply disabled must be flagged to owner). This is the one actual billing error found. Remaining work: draft final report distinguishing real vs apparent errors, list refund-promise retraction",
